From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreXGT <aulia.ikbal09@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor: keep the vendor ICU on cm-14.1, drop it on cm-13.0

cm-13.0 only.

The MIUI libicuuc.so must NOT overwrite the platform's own ICU 55.1 on
cm-13.0: the platform also builds libicui18n from that ICU and the two
builds are not ABI compatible (the platform's libicui18n references the
icu_55 C++ vtables, which the MIUI ICU build does not have):

    CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE: cannot locate symbol
    "_ZTVN6icu_5512CacheKeyBaseE" referenced by "/system/lib/libicui18n.so"

That library is in the LD_PRELOAD chain (libmtk_symbols.so), so the
failure hit every process init started and the device bootlooped into
recovery.

On cm-14.1 the vendor ICU has to stay: that platform ships ICU 58 and
the MTK blobs need the ICU-55 flavour (the icu55.c shim in
libmtk_symbols provides the ICU-55 entry points).

The filter-out is kept on a single line on purpose.  A hand written
patch of this file had a wrong hunk line count ("@@ -1,2 +1,13 @@" for a
hunk that carried 14 new lines); git apply silently dropped the last line
of the hunk, which left the filter-out call unterminated and the build
died with

    build/core/node_fns.mk:185: *** unterminated call to function
    'filter-out': missing ')'.  Stop.

This patch is therefore generated from "git diff" so that the hunk counts
are always exact, and the call is written on one line so that a dropped
continuation line cannot break it a second time.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000008
---
 nikel-vendor-blobs.mk | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nikel-vendor-blobs.mk b/nikel-vendor-blobs.mk
index ce48c16..f4f4806 100755
--- a/nikel-vendor-blobs.mk
+++ b/nikel-vendor-blobs.mk
@@ -1,2 +1,12 @@
-PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-	$(call find-copy-subdir-files,*,vendor/xiaomi/nikel/system/,system/)
+# The MIUI libicuuc.so must not overwrite the platform's own ICU on cm-13.0:
+# the platform builds libicui18n from that ICU and the two builds are not
+# ABI compatible (the platform's libicui18n references the icu_55 C++
+# vtables, which the MIUI ICU build does not have).  On cm-14.1 the vendor
+# ICU has to stay - that platform ships ICU 58 and the MTK blobs need the
+# ICU-55 flavour (the icu55.c shim in libmtk_symbols provides it).
+VENDOR_ICU_BLACKLIST :=
+ifeq ($(PLATFORM_VERSION),6.0.1)
+VENDOR_ICU_BLACKLIST := %:system/lib/libicuuc.so %:system/lib64/libicuuc.so
+endif
+
+PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += $(filter-out $(VENDOR_ICU_BLACKLIST),$(call find-copy-subdir-files,*,vendor/xiaomi/nikel/system/,system/))
